BIT-09: Linear wall shift, new segments only when added, one allocation each

shiftSegWallQual() restarted its inner loop from the pipe's upstream end
for every segment, O(n^2) in the segments of a pipe; make it one pass.
advectSegs() took and zeroed a new segment for every link at every step,
though the inflow usually merges into the last segment; take one only when
a segment is added. Allocate a segment and its two concentration arrays in
one block.

Requires: FIX-02
Results: identical (every concentration, the output file and the report are unchanged)

Apply from the root of an EPANET-MSX checkout at 85a303d, after FIX-01, FIX-02 and BIT-01 to BIT-08:
    git apply --whitespace=nowarn BIT-09.patch
or use tools/build-msx.sh, which applies the series in order.

